Why this licence and not a permissive one
-----------------------------------------

Not a choice. The text base this project fine-tunes inherits CC-BY-NC-4.0 from
its training corpus, and that restriction passes to every derivative, including
this repository's code, the checkpoints, and the listening material. Nothing
here may be used commercially.

To change that you would have to replace the text base's training data with a
corpus whose licence permits commercial use, and read the terms of the frozen
components. Relaxing this statement without doing that would be a false claim.


What is not ours
----------------

The audio architecture comes from MiniMind-O (Apache-2.0), and files derived
from it keep their upstream notices. The audio codec is Mimi (CC-BY-4.0), which
requires attribution and is pinned by revision. The speaker encoder is CAM++
(Apache-2.0). Two further components are relied on but not redistributed here:
SenseVoice and emotion2vec, both under the FunASR Model Open Source License
Agreement v1.1, which has no clear redistribution clause.

Four assets carry declarations we could not verify -- upstream's Talker
weights, the MiniMind-O training data, SenseVoice and emotion2vec. Each one is
recorded with what its card claims, why we did not take that at face value, and
what would settle it, in:

    configs/release/licence.json

That file is the authority. This one is the summary.
